## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design at scale with multi-tenancy, data privacy, and production observability.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time ingestion, per-tenant DP feasibility, idempotent processing, multi-tenant S3 prefixes, OpenTelemetry instrumentation, cost controls.

## Code Example
```javascript
// budget-enforcement.js
async function enforceBudget(tenantId, epsilon) {
  const budget = await db.get(`dp-budget:${tenantId}`)
  if (budget.remaining < epsilon) throw new Error('Budget exhausted')
  await db.update(`dp-budget:${tenantId}`, { remaining: budget.remaining - epsilon })
}
```

Why This Is Asked
 Assesses ability to design a cross-region, tenant-isolated telemetry path with tracing across all stages, enforcing exactly-once semantics, SLA verification, and late data handling.

Key Concepts
 - OpenTelemetry trace propagation across producers, compute, and batch jobs
 - Exactly-once processing and idempotence per tenant
 - Cross-region data flow and a DynamoDB backplane for traces
 - Tenant isolation via partition keys and quotas
 - Late data handling and robust testing strategy

Code Example
